# What SITL's telemetry ports stream, in messages per second: SERIAL0, which sends to
# the gateway over UDP, and SERIAL2 (TCP 5763), which the gateway can connect to with
# -input tcp:127.0.0.1:5763. SERIAL1 is left to fly.py, which asks for its own streams.
#
# The gateway never sends, so it cannot ask for streams the way a ground station does;
# the autopilot has to be told here. ArduPilot 4.7 calls these MAVn_*, numbered over
# the MAVLink ports in order: MAV1 is SERIAL0 and MAV3 is SERIAL2. Older firmware
# called them SRn_*, numbered from SR0.
#
# 10 Hz for the timed samples the gateway stamps messages with, so a 10 Hz gateway
# always has a fresh one:
#   POSITION  GLOBAL_POSITION_INT       EXTRA1  ATTITUDE        EXTRA2  VFR_HUD
#   EXT_STAT  SYS_STATUS, GPS_RAW_INT   EXTRA3  SYSTEM_TIME, BATTERY_STATUS
MAV1_POSITION 10
MAV1_EXTRA1 10
MAV1_EXTRA2 10
MAV1_EXT_STAT 2
MAV1_EXTRA3 2
MAV1_RAW_SENS 0
MAV1_RC_CHAN 0
MAV1_RAW_CTRL 0
MAV1_ADSB 0
MAV3_POSITION 10
MAV3_EXTRA1 10
MAV3_EXTRA2 10
MAV3_EXT_STAT 2
MAV3_EXTRA3 2
MAV3_RAW_SENS 0
MAV3_RC_CHAN 0
MAV3_RAW_CTRL 0
MAV3_ADSB 0
